Flutter is an open-source UI toolkit developed by Google for building beautiful, natively compiled applications for mobile, web, and 
desktop from a single codebase using the Dart programming language.

"Flutter is a framework used to create mobile, web, and desktop applications using a single codebase."
    - Developed by Google
    - Uses Dart language
    - Single codebase for Android, iOS, Web, Windows, macOS, and Linux
    - Fast development with Hot Reload
    - Rich collection of widgets for building UI

syntax:
     import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

          void main() {
                 runApp(MyApp());
          }

import → Imports Flutter library.
main() → Starting point of the app.
runApp() → Runs the Flutter app.
MyApp() → Your first widget.
